    "limitations": [
      "Independently re-observed opaque-contour successor: Shrimp landmarks and priority ownership on the retained dorsal master. Five real walking chains are observed separately on each side; no hidden legs are inferred.",
      "Far/Near are stable upper/lower image-side identifiers in this dorsal projection, not a claim that the camera sees lateral depth. Leg root/knee/foot are coarse controls at observed attachment, bend and terminal paint.",
      "The full leg painting is retained. The three-joint template does not represent every biological segment; painted additional bends remain on their source chain.",
      "The actual two eyes, short antennules, swimmerets and small rostral structures remain painted under the continuous head/abdominal owners. No extra template joint, appendage deletion or absent declaration is invented.",
      "The dorsal view exposes the anatomical chains but does not provide a common ground-contact line. groundLineY records the painted lower walking-tip envelope only; swimming and crawling motion require full-size review.",
      "Long antennae cross anterior structures in the source; visibility at crossings is limited to the painted topmost contour. The declared owners and software motion review must retain any cut-gap hold.",
      "All originals and painting-side framing successors remain separate; source preservation is exact to this selected successor, not an assertion that the generator preserved predecessor pixels.",
      "No reference-pool, native or family-wide admission.",
      "C196 bounded successor to the rejected widened-root candidate: retain exact C192 proximal leg/body polygons and all joints. Only observed distal leg contours and antenna endpoints receive the traced source paint.",
